{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>She is more righteous than I.</b> Even though she came to me by deception and I did not recognize her at all, for I sent the kid — nevertheless she is righteous in her deception, for it was for the sake of a good and desirable end before the blessed El, namely the perpetuation of the seed, not for her own gratification, since she immediately returned to her widowhood. She is more righteous than I, for my fulfillment of my pledge had as its intent my own honor and the recovery of my pledge, which is a deficient and inferior end, as they said, of blessed memory (Nazir 23b): גְּדוֹלָה עֲבֵרָה לִשְׁמָהּ מִמִּצְוָה שֶׁלֹּא לִשְׁמָהּ (\"a transgression for its own sake is greater than a commandment not for its own sake\")."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:53.819078150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}